     <narrative xml:lang="EN">This DE aims to enhance the capacities of the HDCs in managing agricultural services decentralized with the CHT Peace Accord and subsequent legal reforms - 33 functions and powers are to be transferred to the HDCs as per the Peace Accord, including agricultural services. On paper, these power and functions have already been transferred from the line ministries/agencies to the HDCs. However, the HDCs have still not managed to take full ownership of the transferred functions. With the capacities of the HDCs enhanced, the envisaged outcomes will be: improved coordination and management functions, including regulatory framework of HDCs to manage transferred agricultural services. Important linkages are to be established and actions coordinated between the HDC, the Upazila and Union Parishads and the target communities concerning development of Union level Local Resilience Plans against climate change. UNDP will play a role as promoter and facilitator in this process.</narrative>
    </title>
